// Detection: Persistence via scheduled task
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1053.005 - Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task
// Data source: SecurityEvent (Windows Security Event Log via Azure Monitor Agent)
// Trigger event: 4698 (A scheduled task was created)

SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4698
| extend TaskName = extractjson("$.TaskName", TaskContentXML)
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, Account = SubjectAccount, TaskName, TaskContentXML
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// Tuning notes:
// - Baseline legitimate scheduled task creation (software updaters, backup
//   jobs) before enabling as an alert to avoid noisy false positives.
// - Flag tasks whose action executes from unusual paths (%TEMP%, %APPDATA%,
//   user-writable directories) or references encoded/obfuscated commands
//   as higher-severity.
// - Consider a companion query on EventID 4699 (task deleted) / 4702 (task
//   updated) to catch defense-evasion cleanup after persistence is achieved.
